    <semantic:process id="_3edab1fe-9ee3-430c-9a53-e5e33a9f4a6f" name="advanced" triso:readOnly="false" triso:collectEnds="true" isClosed="false">
        <semantic:textAnnotation id="_4844db0e-88c5-4a0c-83a8-9a9c771be57b">
            <semantic:text>Today's concept: Activity: the unit of work. In a mobile game in-app purchase scenario, ask: What starts the flow, where can it split, how does it rejoin, and what ends it? Name tasks verb-object and avoid crossing lines. If a decision is needed, pick the gateway that matches the semantics. If data crosses pools, use a message flow, not a sequence flow. Keep one clear idea per diagram. Here's the one-sentence way to remember it: make it obvious, and test it with token animation if your tool supports it. Open your modeler and build a tiny demo.</semantic:text>
        </semantic:textAnnotation>
    </semantic:process>
